# The burgomaster's burial, at the open grave in the churchyard (started from Ismark, Ireena or Donavich at the
# grave, or from Parriwimple's graveside line). Ends with Strahd at the lych-gate, or Doru if he was freed.
# Defying or attacking Strahd, or a hasty burial, starts churchyard_dead. The escort choice follows in
# ireena.dialogue (after_burial).

~ start
Narrator: The coffin rests on two trestles beside the open grave. Behind every shutter on the lane someone is watching, and none of them came.
if flag.parriwimple_pallbearer
Parriwimple: I dug it deep. Six feet. I measured with my arm, twice. Then I made it a little deeper, for the wolves.
endif
Ireena: Let's begin. Before the light goes.
if flag.donavich_will_officiate and not flag.donavich_refused_rites and not (flag.doru_destroyed and not flag.donavich_mercy_blessing)
-> priest_rites
endif
-> no_priest

~ priest_rites
set burial_method = "church_rites"
Donavich: We give Kolyan Indirovich to the earth he kept, in the light he trusted. Morninglord, you who come back every morning though no one thanks you for it, come back for him.
if flag.doru_destroyed or flag.doru_freed
-> rites_done
endif
Narrator: From under the church, faint through the stone, a voice howls for its father. Donavich's prayer breaks in half.
Donavich [afraid]: Forgive me. Forgive... I've lost the words.
* [Religion DC 12] Take up the prayer where he lost it. -> rites_steadied | rites_stumble
* [Cleric] Pray with him, one voice under his. -> rites_steadied
* Wait for him to find his voice. -> rites_stumble

~ rites_steadied
attitude donavich friendly
Narrator: Your voice catches his and carries it. He finds the next line, and the next, and the howling below fades under the two of you.
-> rites_done

~ rites_stumble
Narrator: He stands silent a long moment while the howling goes on. Then he finishes the prayer in a whisper, very fast, as if afraid it won't let him.
-> rites_done

~ rites_done
Donavich: Rest, Kolyan. Nobody will call you up again. Not while I have breath to forbid it.
-> lowered

~ no_priest
if flag.donavich_will_officiate
Ismark [weary]: Donavich isn't coming. After what happened under his church, I can't say I blame him.
endif
Ismark [weary]: No priest, then. Someone say something. Father would hate a silent funeral; he never let a silence pass without a speech.
* [Cleric] Speak the rites of your own faith over him. -> cleric_rites
* [Religion DC 12] Recite the Morninglord's burial prayer, as best you can. -> lay_rites_ok | lay_rites_fail
* Say a few honest words of your own. -> lay_rites_honest
* Fill in the grave. There's no time for words. -> hasty

~ cleric_rites
set burial_method = "cleric_rites"
attitude ireena friendly
interject class:cleric: Earth to earth, and the dark to the dawn. Rest, Kolyan Indirovich. Let no voice call you up again.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Rest easy, sir. We'll look after her. On my oath.
Narrator: The words aren't the ones this village uses, but they're said with care, and the earth seems to accept them.
inspire class:cleric: spoke the rites over Kolyan Indirovich
approve liriel_dawnsong +2: You gave Kolyan the rites of your own faith
-> lowered

~ lay_rites_ok
set burial_method = "lay_rites"
Narrator: You stumble through the old prayer, half-remembered from church doors in other countries, and Ireena mouths the parts you miss. Between you, it's whole.
-> lowered

~ lay_rites_fail
set burial_method = "lay_rites"
Narrator: The prayer comes out in the wrong order, and the last verse leaves you entirely. Ireena finishes it, quietly, without looking up.
-> lowered

~ lay_rites_honest
set burial_method = "lay_rites"
Narrator: You say what you can about a man you never met: that he held his door every night until his heart gave out. It's short, and Ismark nods as if it were the right length.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +1 thistle +1: You said a few honest words over a man you never met
-> lowered

~ hasty
set burial_method = "hasty"
attitude ireena indifferent
Ireena [angry]: No words. Fine. Fill it in, then. Quickly, since that's how you like it.
Narrator: The earth goes in fast and badly, and nobody speaks. Somewhere beyond the wall, something laughs, softly.
approve liriel_dawnsong -3 godrick_pendlebrook -2 kip_smudgewick -1: You filled in Kolyan's grave without a word
-> lowered

~ lowered
set burgomaster_buried
quest bury_the_burgomaster buried
quest escort_ireena ready
if flag.doru_destroyed
quest the_priests_son doru_destroyed
endif
Ireena [sad]: Goodbye, Father. You found me on a road. I'm going back to one. I'll try to be worth the finding.
Ismark: Rest, old man. I'll look after her. I'll do better than I did.
xp milestone
if flag.doru_freed
-> doru_messenger
endif
-> strahd_arrives

~ strahd_arrives
set strahd_met
appear strahd at lych_gate
cutscene burial_strahd
Narrator: The air turns cold enough to fog your breath. At the lych-gate, where nobody stood a moment ago, a tall man in a fine black coat waits, hat in hand, like a mourner who came late.
Strahd: Do not stop on my account. Kolyan shouted at my wolves from his doorway every night for a month. Let him have a little quiet now. He had none at the end.
Ireena [angry]: Get out of here.
Strahd [smile]: I am at the gate, my dear, as a guest should be. Everything past it is mine: the yard, the grave, the man in it. And you. Keep the scarf on. I know what is under it. I put it there.
if flag.ireena_bite_seen
Narrator: Ireena's hand goes to the scarf at her throat before she can stop it. He sees, and his smile widens.
endif
if flag.ilse_invitation_shown
Strahd: And the soldier who kept my invitation. I am touched. Your company asked after you, you know. Near the end.
interject name:ilse_varga: Where are they.
if name:ilse_varga and not (quest.kestrel_company >= the_host)
quest kestrel_company the_host
endif
endif
if flag.tamsin_locket_recognized
Strahd [sly]: The little thief carries her portrait. Keep it close, child. When I want it back, I will come for it, and for the hand that holds it.
endif
if name:liriel_dawnsong
Strahd: A priestess of the dawn, in my valley. How brave. How very late.
endif
if name:wren_featherfoot
Strahd: And a little monk who stands like a dusk elf. I knew a whole people who stood like that. There are very few of them left. I saw to it.
endif
if name:kip_smudgewick
Strahd [smile]: And you, merchant. You smell of brimstone and apricots. Someone already holds your paper. I wonder what they would take for it.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: It's, er. It's a small business matter. Lovely to meet you, sir.
endif
if class:wizard
Strahd: And a scholar. My library would delight you. You must come up and see it. The last scholar who came is up there still. He has stopped asking to leave.
endif
if flag.vistani_spies_suspected
interject tag:curious: So that's who the Vistani tell their stories to.
endif
Strahd: I came to welcome you to my land, all of you. You have been busy since you came, and I know every door you have knocked on. Stay as long as you like. The mists will see that you do.
-> strahd_menu

~ strahd_menu
* Ireena is under our protection. Leave. -> defiant
* [Intimidation DC 20] Come one step closer and find out what we're capable of. -> threat_ok | threat_fail
* What do you want with her? -> what_want
* Bow, and answer him with courtesy. -> courteous
* Attack him. -> violent
* Say nothing. -> silent

~ what_want
Strahd: What is mine. Ireena knows the way home. She has always known it; she has only forgotten. I will remind her, one night at a time.
Ireena [afraid]: I don't know what he means. I don't. Don't look at me like that.
-> strahd_menu

~ defiant
set strahd_first_impression = "defiant"
Strahd [smile]: Under your protection. Kolyan said the same, from his doorway, with a lamp. It held for a month. Let us see whether yours does better.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +2 thistle +2 wren_featherfoot +1 kip_smudgewick -1: You told Strahd to his face that Ireena was under your protection
-> ismark_choked

~ threat_ok
set strahd_first_impression = "defiant"
Narrator: For the barest instant something flickers behind his courtesy: not fear, but attention. He looks at you as if you have just become interesting.
if flag.death_house_completed
Strahd: Yes. You did well in that house. Let us see you do well here.
else
Strahd: Perhaps you are. Let us find out.
endif
approve thistle +2 kip_smudgewick -2 ratatoille -1: You threatened Strahd across a grave
-> ismark_choked

~ threat_fail
set strahd_first_impression = "defiant"
Strahd [smile]: Well said. The last man who shouted at me is in that grave. Allow me to return the courtesy.
approve thistle +2 kip_smudgewick -2 ratatoille -1: You threatened Strahd across a grave
-> ismark_choked

~ courteous
set strahd_first_impression = "courteous"
Strahd [smile]: Manners. Good. You will need them at my table, and my guests do not always leave it. We will speak again. Ireena. Leave the window unlatched tonight. I should hate to break the glass.
Narrator: The mist thickens at the gate, and then he isn't there.
vanish strahd
Ireena [angry]: Courtesy. To him.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1 kip_smudgewick +1 ratatoille +1 thistle -2 wren_featherfoot -1 godrick_pendlebrook -1: You bowed to Strahd and answered him politely
-> after_strahd

~ violent
set strahd_first_impression = "violent"
Narrator: Steel and spell reach the lych-gate together and pass through cold mist. His laughter comes from everywhere at once.
Strahd: Steel, at a funeral. Here, then: something you are allowed to kill. They were this village's grandmothers once. Do be gentle.
approve thistle +1 kip_smudgewick -3 ratatoille -2: You attacked Strahd at the lych-gate
-> ismark_choked

~ silent
set strahd_first_impression = "silent"
Strahd: Silence. Wise. Keep it; I will learn what you love without asking. Ireena. Latch the window, if it helps you sleep. It will not stop me.
-> ismark_choked

~ ismark_choked
set ismark_choked
Narrator: Strahd turns his eyes on Ismark. Nothing more. Ismark's hand flies to his throat, and he goes down on his knees in the grave dirt, mouth working, blood running from his nose into his beard.
Strahd: Your father held his door for a month with a lamp, Ismark. You could not hold a cup.
Ireena [afraid]: Stop it! Please. Please, he can't breathe!
Strahd: Since you ask it, my dear. You see how easily I give you things, when you ask.
if flag.strahd_first_impression == "silent"
Narrator: Ismark drags in a breath like a man pulled out of a river. When he can lift his head, the gate is empty and the mist is thinning.
vanish strahd
-> after_strahd
endif
Narrator: Ismark drags in a breath like a man pulled out of a river. Before he can get up off his knees, all around the churchyard the earth begins to split.
-> rise

~ after_strahd
if flag.burial_method == "hasty"
Narrator: The quiet lasts a breath; then the hasty grave shifts, and every old grave around it answers. Unblessed earth, it seems, is an open door.
-> rise
endif
-> village_of_barovia/ireena:after_burial

~ rise
vanish strahd
vanish doru
cutscene burial_graves
Ismark: Ireena, behind me! Into the church porch, go!
combat churchyard_dead

~ doru_messenger
appear doru at lych_gate
cutscene burial_doru
Narrator: Something perches on the churchyard wall like a crow: Doru, his cheeks full now, his lips red, smiling.
Doru [smile]: Don't stop. I like funerals now. My master sends his regrets; he's dining elsewhere tonight. He says Ireena should leave her window open. It's stuffy, waiting.
Ireena [afraid]: Doru? Oh, Doru. No.
* Tell your master the answer is no. -> doru_defy
* Doru. Your father is still praying for you. -> doru_father
* Attack him. -> doru_attack

~ doru_defy
set strahd_first_impression = "defiant"
Doru [sly]: I'll tell him. He'll smile. He smiled at us too, all through dinner. He sent a gift, in case you said it.
Narrator: Doru drops backward off the wall and is gone. Behind you, the old graves begin to split.
-> rise

~ doru_father
Doru [sad]: Is he. Is he still. Tell him... no. Tell him nothing. Tell him I was never here.
Narrator: For a moment he's only a young man on a wall. Then he isn't there at all.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1 wren_featherfoot +1: You told Doru his father still prays for him
-> after_strahd

~ doru_attack
Narrator: He's off the wall before your weapons clear, laughing, and the laughter comes from the dark between the graves, where the earth has started to move.
-> rise
